ally  settle out of court so if there was a  rare instance where i didn't feel like  the client had a a leg to stand on  then almost certainly that client uh  would have  settled and and gotten out of the  lawsuit that way  if you get into multi-million dollar  litigation  and you keep going forward and you get  to trial the reason that you're in trial  is because both sides  think they can win so that's actually  the rarity to actually  get that far into a case for the most  part  if people were did something wrong  they're going to settle and try and get  out as quickly as possible  sergey niskanen says how can one become  a judge are there some special law  schools for that or is it more a  question of long-term legal practice and  general experience  or maybe there are some very specific  requirements have you ever considered a  judicial career for yourself  uh so how do you become a judge well  that depends on the jurisdiction  some are appointed by the governor or  the president and some  are elected depends on where you live  and the particular court you're dealing  with  no special law schools any law school  will do though  going to a higher ranked law school  makes you more likely to become  a judge i would probably say though when  you are appointed to be a judge often  certain states and the federal system  will send you to judge school because  often people don't know what they're  doing and sort of a crash course and  actually being a judge so technically  there is sort of a special  judge school and i have absolutely no  aspirations of becoming a judge myself  i am very very thankful that we have a  lot of good judges out there but that is  definitely not something i would want to  do myself  all right let's uh let's do some rapid  fire questions i think i've been taking  this  way too seriously and i want to get  through a bunch more of these questions  so let's let's try and do it  christopher miller asks when did it  become comfortable speaking in 