ng this one  yes idiot asks since you've looked at a  lot of legal movies  what do you think makes a legal movie  enjoyable while still being accurate  while i am happy to criticize legal  movies for their accuracy  legal accuracy is not the most important  thing for me when i'm watching a legal  movie i think the dialogue needs to be  good and most importantly  the characters need to grow basically  everything that happens in the plot is  really just in service of  helping the protagonist or the  antagonist grow as a person  and that i think is the most important  thing sometimes legal accuracy totally  gets in the way of that  but sometimes you'll get a show like  better call saul that is able to tell  amazing stories while still being  legally accurate and that's super cool  too  cool guy not full guy asks stupid  question but why did you choose the name  legal eagle  because eagles are cool and it rhymes  and as one of the comments pointed out  unlawful falafel  doesn't have the same ring to it okay  edward zhang asks to add to the question  of your specialty in law what made you  decide on this particular specialty i'm  a prospective law student and having a  hard time figuring out what i want to  specialize in well  in a way i haven't really specialized i  am  a litigator and trial lawyer so i guess  my specialty is the process the process  of  the lawsuit the process of going to  trial but in terms of the substantive  law that i deal with  it has varied widely it includes  copyrighting  includes class action defense it  includes contracts business  ip banking and it's great that every day  i get to research something new it keeps  things fresh and that's one of the  things i love about this particular  channel is that  i get to do research into new parts of  the law to become a momentary expert  about these particular things so that i  can explain  the law to other people so in some ways  i haven't had to specialize and  that's one of the things that i think 